110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 190 0 R
/T (Key Question: How can we train machines to understand diverse forms of human communication and bridge the accessibility gap? )
/E (Key Question: How can we train machines to understand diverse forms of human communication and bridge the accessibility gap? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 190 0 R
/T (Non-Technical Explanation: Most human-robot interaction relies heavily on spoken language or standard text inputs. For the deaf and hard-of-hearing community, this creates a massive barrier. By training Machine Learning \(ML\) models on visual data, we can teach robots to recognize and interpret sign language gestures in real time. )
/E (Non-Technical Explanation: Most human-robot interaction relies heavily on spoken language or standard text inputs. For the deaf and hard-of-hearing community, this creates a massive barrier. By training Machine Learning \(ML\) models on visual data, we can teach robots to recognize and interpret sign language gestures in real time. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Activity: The Sign Language Detection Demo & Stress Test \(30 min\): Students interact with a live Machine Learning demo designed to detect sign language gestures. They will analyze its performance and run a "bias and limitation check": )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 342 0 R
/E (The Test: Perform standard sign gestures. Does the model recognize them accurately? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 343 0 R
