/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 344 0 R
/E (The Analysis: Does the model perform equally well for everyone? What happens if the training dataset lacked diverse representation \(e.g., different skin colors, hand shapes, or lighting\)? )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Goal: Understand that an ML model is only as fair as its training data. If we want robots to ensure equal rights to all when communicating, we must actively prevent algorithmic exclusion.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
