134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 358 0 R
/E (Talking to a Robot with Your Hands: Instead of typing or speaking, students get to use their physical body and gestures to control or communicate with a machine. It feels like unlocking a "superpower" or a secret language code.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 359 0 R
/E (Playing the "System Breaker": Young people love to see where technology fails. The activity actively encourages them to try and "trick" or "break" the AI by changing lighting, hiding fingers, or using different angles, turning data analysis into a game of discovery.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
